## Web demo defaults

```
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
# Optional corpus deep links for citation tiles
VITE_DOCUMENTS_PUBLIC_BASE=https://demo-host.example/files
#
# UI-only dev path. When `true`, the Ask BPL chat surface returns canned
# answer / refusal / PII responses instead of POSTing to the orchestrator —
# useful for visual QA of Wireframe v3 without provisioning Pinecone /
# Anthropic / Selvon keys. The same toggle is available per-page-load via
# `?mock=ask` on the host URL.
# VITE_MOCK_ASK=true
#
# Re-enable the legacy draggable Spline-capable avatar shell. Default is
# off — the wireframe v3 modal is the demo-ready surface. Turn this on to
# revisit the avatar work in `avatar/AvatarShellLegacy.tsx`.
# VITE_ENABLE_AVATAR_SHELL=true
#
# Skip Spline bundle — book emoji only (slow networks / pilot table demos).
# Only relevant when `VITE_ENABLE_AVATAR_SHELL=true`.
# VITE_LITE_DEMO=true
#
# Mount the real Spline scene (WebGL). Leave unset for SVG-book avatar — some GPUs lose the
# whole tab (~1s after opening the modal) when Spline loads; set only when testing the .splinecode asset.
# Only relevant when `VITE_ENABLE_AVATAR_SHELL=true`.
# VITE_ENABLE_SPLINE=true
```

Copy to `.env.local` (ignored from git).
